window.OT_EMS_SETTING_HELP = {"boil2hystoff":{"e32":"Not used by OpenThermostat. Not offered for modulating boilers.","expect":"Only two-stage burners, mostly older floor-standing oil or gas boilers, use this. On a modulating wall-hung boiler nothing should change.","level":"installer","offer":"never","risk":"A large margin lets the second stage overheat the water before it stops.","what":"Switch-off margin for the second stage of a two-stage burner."},"boil2hyston":{"e32":"Not used by OpenThermostat. Not offered for modulating boilers.","expect":"Only two-stage burners, mostly older floor-standing oil or gas boilers, use this. On a modulating wall-hung boiler nothing should change.","level":"installer","offer":"never","risk":"As for the first stage: a small margin means many starts of the second stage.","what":"Restart margin for the second stage of a two-stage burner."},"boilhystoff":{"e32":"Not controlled by OpenThermostat. Keep this margin in mind when you set the maximum for floor heating.","expect":"A larger margin: longer burns and fewer starts, but hotter water than asked for and a warmer return, so slightly less condensing.","level":"installer","offer":"candidate","risk":"A large margin can push the flow above what a floor heating circuit should get.","what":"How far the water to the heating may rise above its target before the burner switches off (switching margin, hysteresis)."},"boilhyston":{"e32":"Not controlled by OpenThermostat. Its own flow request changes slowly, which already limits starts.","expect":"A larger margin: fewer starts and longer burns, but the water temperature swings more. A smaller one: a steadier temperature and more starts.","level":"installer","offer":"candidate","risk":"A margin close to zero makes the boiler short-cycle when little heat is needed.","what":"How far the water to the heating must drop below its target before the burner starts again (switching margin, hysteresis)."},"burnmaxpower":{"e32":"OpenThermostat does not limit burner power.","expect":"Lower: slower, steadier heating and a slightly cooler flue, which suits an oversized boiler. It does not lower the burner's minimum, so it does not stop on-off cycling at low demand.","level":"installer","offer":"candidate","risk":"Too low and the house cannot be kept warm on the coldest days. Hot water on a combi boiler may have its own limit.","what":"Caps the burner power for heating, as a percentage of what the boiler can deliver."},"burnminperiod":{"e32":"OpenThermostat already keeps its own minimum on and off time for its request. This boiler timer works inside a running request.","expect":"Longer: fewer burner starts, less wear and steadier running. The water may cool a bit further before the boiler starts again.","level":"installer","offer":"candidate","risk":"Very short times let the boiler switch on and off often (short cycling). Very long times make rooms react slowly, especially with radiators.","what":"The shortest time the burner waits before it may start again for heating (anti-cycling)."},"dhw.activated":{"e32":"OpenThermostat does not control hot water.","expect":"Off: no gas for hot water and no keep-warm runs, but also no hot water. A circulation pump stops as well.","level":"user","offer":"candidate","risk":"A hot water store that stays cold for days can grow bacteria (legionella). Heat it fully once before you use it again.","what":"Allows or blocks hot water heating by the boiler."},"dhw.chargeoptimization":{"e32":"Not controlled by OpenThermostat. Not offered until it is confirmed per model.","expect":"On: slightly less gas per charge. The store may end just below its target.","level":"installer","offer":"candidate","risk":"Hardly documented. On some boilers this value used to be read as a hysteresis, so its effect must be checked per model.","what":"While the store charges, the burner stops a little early and the pump finishes the job with the heat that is left."},"dhw.circ":{"e32":"Not controlled by OpenThermostat. A command, so it is not offered as a setting.","expect":"On: hot water reaches the taps sooner for a while. The boiler's own schedule takes over again later.","level":"user","offer":"action","risk":"Little risk. It only costs some heat from the pipes.","what":"Switches the circulation pump on or off now. It is a command, not a stored setting. On this page the row shows whether the pump runs."},"dhw.circmode":{"e32":"Not controlled by OpenThermostat.","expect":"More often: hot water at the tap sooner, but more heat lost from the pipes and more reheating of the store. Running all the time costs the most.","level":"installer","offer":"candidate","risk":"Only matters when a circulation pump is fitted. Long pauses leave lukewarm water standing in the pipes.","what":"How often the circulation pump runs: off, 1 to 6 times 3 minutes per hour, or all the time."},"dhw.circpump":{"e32":"Not controlled by OpenThermostat.","expect":"Off: the circulation pump never runs. That saves heat lost in the pipes, but hot water takes longer to reach the tap.","level":"installer","offer":"candidate","risk":"Switching it on without a pump fitted does nothing useful. Long unused circulation pipes can hold lukewarm water.","what":"Tells the boiler whether a hot water circulation pump is fitted and may run."},"dhw.comfort1":{"e32":"OpenThermostat does not control hot water, but the Boiler page counts keep-warm runs, so you can see the effect.","expect":"Eco: fewer keep-warm runs and less gas per day, mostly when little hot water is used. Hot water may take longer or run lukewarm sooner.","level":"user","offer":"candidate","risk":"Eco together with a low hot water temperature keeps the store longer in the range where bacteria grow.","what":"Comfort keeps hot water ready all the time. Eco heats less often and first lets the water cool further."},"dhw.disinfecting":{"e32":"Not controlled by OpenThermostat. Not offered while it cannot be stopped safely.","expect":"Much more gas for one run, and very hot water at the taps for hours.","level":"installer","offer":"never","risk":"Risk of scalding. EMS-ESP notes that stopping it this way does not seem to work; switching the boiler off and on stops it.","what":"Starts a thermal disinfection now: the boiler heats the hot water to the disinfection temperature and holds it there for a while. On this page the row shows whether one runs."},"dhw.disinfectiontemp":{"e32":"Not controlled by OpenThermostat.","expect":"Only matters while a disinfection runs. Higher: a shorter hold time, but more gas and more scale.","level":"installer","offer":"candidate","risk":"During and after a disinfection the tap water can be hot enough to scald.","what":"The temperature the boiler uses when it runs a thermal disinfection (against legionella) of the hot water."},"dhw.flowtempoffset":{"e32":"Not controlled by OpenThermostat.","expect":"Lower: the store charges more slowly, but the boiler condenses more. Higher: hot water is back sooner after a shower.","level":"installer","offer":"candidate","risk":"Too low and the store may never reach its target, which also weakens the protection against bacteria.","what":"How much hotter than the hot water target the boiler makes its own water while it charges the store."},"dhw.hyston":{"e32":"Not controlled by OpenThermostat. The Boiler page counts keep-warm runs, so you can see the effect.","expect":"A larger margin: fewer, longer reheats and less gas lost to short keep-warm runs. The store is cooler just before a reheat.","level":"installer","offer":"candidate","risk":"A large margin with a low target keeps the store in the range where bacteria grow. A small one gives many short burner runs.","what":"How far the water in the store must cool below its target before the boiler heats it again."},"dhw.onetime":{"e32":"Not controlled by OpenThermostat. A command: it could later become a button, not a setting.","expect":"One extra reheat. Handy before a bath when eco is on.","level":"user","offer":"action","risk":"Little risk. It costs the gas of one reheat.","what":"Heats the hot water once to its target now, also in eco mode. On this page the row shows whether such a charge runs."},"dhw.seltemp":{"e32":"OpenThermostat does not control hot water.","expect":"Lower: less gas to keep the store warm and less scale. You get less hot water before it runs lukewarm.","level":"user","offer":"candidate","risk":"Below about 55 °C bacteria (legionella) can grow in a store. Above 60 °C there is a risk of scalding and more scale.","what":"The temperature the boiler keeps the hot water at: the store, or the water from the tap on a combi boiler."},"heatingactivated":{"e32":"OpenThermostat stops asking for heat by itself when no room needs it. It cannot override this switch.","expect":"Off: the boiler ignores every heat request, also from OpenThermostat, until you switch it on again. Useful as a summer switch.","level":"user","offer":"candidate","risk":"While it is off, the house is not protected against frost. Only the boiler protects itself.","what":"Allows or blocks central heating on the boiler itself. Hot water has its own switch."},"heatingtemp":{"e32":"OpenThermostat keeps its own maximum per installation and never asks for more than this boiler limit.","expect":"Lower: radiators and floor stay cooler and the boiler condenses more, so it uses a little less gas. On very cold days the house warms up more slowly.","level":"user","offer":"candidate","risk":"Too low and rooms stay cold in winter. Too high is unsafe for floor heating without its own mixing valve and safety thermostat.","what":"The highest water temperature the boiler sends to the heating, whatever a thermostat asks for."},"pumpdelay":{"e32":"OpenThermostat does not run the pump itself. This is one of the four Classic settings the E32 can read back.","expect":"Longer: the heat left in the boiler reaches the rooms instead of being lost, for a little pump electricity. The 24-hour setting keeps the pump running all the time.","level":"installer","offer":"candidate","risk":"Low risk. A very short time leaves heat behind in the boiler; a very long one only costs electricity.","what":"How long the heating pump keeps running after the heat request ends."},"pumpmode":{"e32":"Not controlled by OpenThermostat.","expect":"A lower fixed pressure saves electricity and reduces flow noise. In the proportional mode the pump slows down when the burner does.","level":"installer","offer":"candidate","risk":"The wrong mode for the system can leave radiators or floor loops short of flow. Not every boiler has a pump that knows these modes.","what":"How the heating pump is controlled: along with the burner power, or at a fixed pressure."},"pumpmodmax":{"e32":"Not controlled by OpenThermostat.","expect":"Lower: a quieter system and less electricity, and often a cooler return that helps condensing. Distant radiators or long floor loops may get too little flow.","level":"installer","offer":"candidate","risk":"Too low and some rooms stay cold, or the boiler reaches its own limit sooner and switches on and off more.","what":"The highest speed the boiler's heating pump may run at."},"pumpmodmin":{"e32":"Not controlled by OpenThermostat.","expect":"Higher: more flow at low power, which helps when distant rooms stay cold. Lower: quieter and less electricity.","level":"installer","offer":"candidate","risk":"Too low can give too little flow. The boiler water then heats up fast and the burner stops early.","what":"The lowest speed the heating pump uses when the boiler runs at low power."},"pumpontemp":{"e32":"Not used by OpenThermostat. Not offered until its meaning is confirmed per model.","expect":"Higher: the boiler first warms itself up, which protects it, but the heat reaches the rooms later.","level":"installer","offer":"never","risk":"On such a boiler a value that is too low may let flue gas condense inside a boiler that is not built for it. What it does on other boilers is unknown.","what":"On low-temperature boilers with a separate boiler controller (such as a Buderus MC10): the boiler temperature the water must reach before the pump starts."},"selburnpow":{"e32":"OpenThermostat sends only a water temperature and leaves this part of the request alone. Never offered.","expect":"The boiler follows the highest power or temperature request it receives. A value set by hand is replaced by the next request.","level":"installer","offer":"never","risk":"A stray power request can keep the burner running when no room needs heat.","what":"The burner power a thermostat asks for right now, as part of the same live heat request."},"selflowtemp":{"e32":"This is OpenThermostat's own heat request. It is never offered as a setting; only the attended boiler test uses it.","expect":"Changing it by hand starts or stops heating at once. OpenThermostat or another thermostat overwrites it within minutes.","level":"installer","offer":"never","risk":"Two devices that send different requests make the boiler switch on and off.","what":"The water temperature a thermostat asks for right now (flow temperature). It is a live request, not a stored setting."}};
(() => {
    const messages = window.OT_UI_MESSAGES = window.OT_UI_MESSAGES || {};
    for (const [key, value] of Object.entries({"A hot water store that stays cold for days can grow bacteria (legionella). Heat it fully once before you use it again.":"Een warmwaterboiler die dagen koud blijft, kan bacteriën (legionella) laten groeien. Warm hem eerst één keer helemaal op voordat je hem weer gebruikt.","A large margin can push the flow above what a floor heating circuit should get.":"Een grote marge kan de aanvoer hoger maken dan een vloerverwarmingsgroep mag krijgen.","A large margin lets the second stage overheat the water before it stops.":"Een grote marge laat de tweede trap het water te warm maken voordat hij stopt.","A large margin with a low target keeps the store in the range where bacteria grow. A small one gives many short burner runs.":"Een grote marge met een laag doel houdt de boiler in het gebied waar bacteriën groeien. Een kleine marge geeft veel korte branderbeurten.","A larger margin: fewer starts and longer burns, but the water temperature swings more. A smaller one: a steadier temperature and more starts.":"Een grotere marge: minder starts en langere branderbeurten, maar de watertemperatuur schommelt meer. Een kleinere marge: een stabielere temperatuur en meer starts.","A larger margin: fewer, longer reheats and less gas lost to short keep-warm runs. The store is cooler just before a reheat.":"Een grotere marge: minder en langere opwarmbeurten en minder gas voor korte warmhoudbeurten. De boiler is vlak voor het opwarmen koeler.","A larger margin: longer burns and fewer starts, but hotter water than asked for and a warmer return, so slightly less condensing.":"Een grotere marge: langere branderbeurten en minder starts, maar warmer water dan gevraagd en een warmere retour, dus iets minder condensatie.","A lower fixed pressure saves electricity and reduces flow noise. In the proportional mode the pump slows down when the burner does.":"Een lagere vaste druk spaart stroom en vermindert stromingsgeluid. In de proportionele stand gaat de pomp langzamer als de brander dat doet.","A margin close to zero makes the boiler short-cycle when little heat is needed.":"Een marge dicht bij nul laat de ketel pendelen als er weinig warmte nodig is.","A stray power request can keep the burner running when no room needs heat.":"Een losse vermogensvraag kan de brander laten branden terwijl geen ruimte warmte nodig heeft.","Allows or blocks central heating on the boiler itself. Hot water has its own switch.":"Staat cv-verwarming op de ketel zelf toe of blokkeert die. Warm water heeft een eigen schakelaar.","Allows or blocks hot water heating by the boiler.":"Staat het opwarmen van warm water door de ketel toe of blokkeert het.","As for the first stage: a small margin means many starts of the second stage.":"Net als bij de eerste trap: een kleine marge geeft veel starts van de tweede trap.","Below about 55 °C bacteria (legionella) can grow in a store. Above 60 °C there is a risk of scalding and more scale.":"Onder ongeveer 55 °C kunnen bacteriën (legionella) groeien in een boiler. Boven 60 °C is er kans op verbranding en meer kalk.","Caps the burner power for heating, as a percentage of what the boiler can deliver.":"Begrenst het brandervermogen voor verwarming, als percentage van wat de ketel kan leveren.","Changing it by hand starts or stops heating at once. OpenThermostat or another thermostat overwrites it within minutes.":"Met de hand wijzigen start of stopt de verwarming direct. OpenThermostat of een andere thermostaat overschrijft het binnen enkele minuten.","Comfort keeps hot water ready all the time. Eco heats less often and first lets the water cool further.":"Comfort houdt warm water steeds klaar. Eco warmt minder vaak op en laat het water eerst verder afkoelen.","During and after a disinfection the tap water can be hot enough to scald.":"Tijdens en na een desinfectie kan het tapwater heet genoeg zijn om je te verbranden.","Eco together with a low hot water temperature keeps the store longer in the range where bacteria grow.":"Eco samen met een lage warmwatertemperatuur houdt de boiler langer in het gebied waar bacteriën groeien.","Eco: fewer keep-warm runs and less gas per day, mostly when little hot water is used. Hot water may take longer or run lukewarm sooner.":"Eco: minder warmhoudbeurten en minder gas per dag, vooral als je weinig warm water gebruikt. Warm water komt mogelijk later of wordt eerder lauw.","Hardly documented. On some boilers this value used to be read as a hysteresis, so its effect must be checked per model.":"Nauwelijks gedocumenteerd. Bij sommige ketels werd deze waarde eerder als hysterese gelezen, dus het effect moet per model gecontroleerd worden.","Heats the hot water once to its target now, also in eco mode. On this page the row shows whether such a charge runs.":"Warmt het warme water nu één keer op tot het doel, ook in de eco-stand. Op deze pagina toont de rij of zo'n oplaadbeurt loopt.","Higher: more flow at low power, which helps when distant rooms stay cold. Lower: quieter and less electricity.":"Hoger: meer doorstroming bij laag vermogen; dat helpt als verre ruimtes koud blijven. Lager: stiller en minder stroom.","Higher: the boiler first warms itself up, which protects it, but the heat reaches the rooms later.":"Hoger: de ketel warmt eerst zichzelf op, wat hem beschermt, maar de warmte komt later in de ruimtes.","How far the water in the store must cool below its target before the boiler heats it again.":"Hoe ver het water in de boiler onder het doel moet afkoelen voordat de ketel het weer opwarmt.","How far the water to the heating may rise above its target before the burner switches off (switching margin, hysteresis).":"Hoe ver het water naar de verwarming boven het doel mag komen voordat de brander uitgaat (schakelmarge, hysterese).","How far the water to the heating must drop below its target before the burner starts again (switching margin, hysteresis).":"Hoe ver het water naar de verwarming onder het doel moet zakken voordat de brander weer start (schakelmarge, hysterese).","How long the heating pump keeps running after the heat request ends.":"Hoe lang de cv-pomp blijft draaien nadat de warmtevraag stopt.","How much hotter than the hot water target the boiler makes its own water while it charges the store.":"Hoeveel warmer dan het warmwaterdoel de ketel zijn eigen water maakt terwijl hij de boiler oplaadt.","How often the circulation pump runs: off, 1 to 6 times 3 minutes per hour, or all the time.":"Hoe vaak de circulatiepomp draait: uit, 1 tot 6 keer 3 minuten per uur, of altijd.","How the heating pump is controlled: along with the burner power, or at a fixed pressure.":"Hoe de cv-pomp geregeld wordt: mee met het brandervermogen, of op een vaste druk.","Little risk. It costs the gas of one reheat.":"Weinig risico. Het kost het gas van één opwarmbeurt.","Little risk. It only costs some heat from the pipes.":"Weinig risico. Het kost alleen wat warmte uit de leidingen.","Longer: fewer burner starts, less wear and steadier running. The water may cool a bit further before the boiler starts again.":"Langer: minder branderstarts, minder slijtage en rustiger bedrijf. Het water koelt iets verder af voordat de ketel opnieuw start.","Longer: the heat left in the boiler reaches the rooms instead of being lost, for a little pump electricity. The 24-hour setting keeps the pump running all the time.":"Langer: de restwarmte in de ketel komt in de ruimtes in plaats van verloren te gaan, voor wat extra pompstroom. De stand 24 uur laat de pomp altijd draaien.","Low risk. A very short time leaves heat behind in the boiler; a very long one only costs electricity.":"Weinig risico. Een erg korte tijd laat warmte achter in de ketel; een erg lange kost alleen stroom.","Lower: a quieter system and less electricity, and often a cooler return that helps condensing. Distant radiators or long floor loops may get too little flow.":"Lager: een stiller systeem en minder stroom, en vaak een koelere retour die condensatie helpt. Verre radiatoren of lange vloergroepen krijgen mogelijk te weinig doorstroming.","Lower: less gas to keep the store warm and less scale. You get less hot water before it runs lukewarm.":"Lager: minder gas om de boiler warm te houden en minder kalk. Je hebt minder warm water voordat het lauw wordt.","Lower: radiators and floor stay cooler and the boiler condenses more, so it uses a little less gas. On very cold days the house warms up more slowly.":"Lager: radiatoren en vloer blijven koeler en de ketel condenseert meer, dus iets minder gas. Op erg koude dagen warmt het huis trager op.","Lower: slower, steadier heating and a slightly cooler flue, which suits an oversized boiler. It does not lower the burner's minimum, so it does not stop on-off cycling at low demand.":"Lager: rustiger en trager verwarmen en een iets koelere rookgasafvoer; dat past bij een te zware ketel. Het verlaagt het minimum van de brander niet, dus aan-uit-pendelen bij weinig vraag blijft.","Lower: the store charges more slowly, but the boiler condenses more. Higher: hot water is back sooner after a shower.":"Lager: de boiler laadt trager op, maar de ketel condenseert meer. Hoger: na het douchen is er sneller weer warm water.","More often: hot water at the tap sooner, but more heat lost from the pipes and more reheating of the store. Running all the time costs the most.":"Vaker: sneller warm water bij de kraan, maar meer warmteverlies uit de leidingen en vaker opwarmen van de boiler. Altijd aan kost het meest.","Much more gas for one run, and very hot water at the taps for hours.":"Veel meer gas voor één keer, en urenlang heel heet water uit de kranen.","Not controlled by OpenThermostat.":"Niet geregeld door OpenThermostat.","Not controlled by OpenThermostat. A command, so it is not offered as a setting.":"Niet geregeld door OpenThermostat. Een opdracht, dus het wordt niet als instelling aangeboden.","Not controlled by OpenThermostat. A command: it could later become a button, not a setting.":"Niet geregeld door OpenThermostat. Een opdracht: het kan later een knop worden, geen instelling.","Not controlled by OpenThermostat. Its own flow request changes slowly, which already limits starts.":"Niet geregeld door OpenThermostat. De eigen aanvoervraag verandert langzaam, wat het aantal starts al beperkt.","Not controlled by OpenThermostat. Keep this margin in mind when you set the maximum for floor heating.":"Niet geregeld door OpenThermostat. Houd rekening met deze marge als je het maximum voor vloerverwarming instelt.","Not controlled by OpenThermostat. Not offered until it is confirmed per model.":"Niet geregeld door OpenThermostat. Niet aangeboden totdat het per model bevestigd is.","Not controlled by OpenThermostat. Not offered while it cannot be stopped safely.":"Niet geregeld door OpenThermostat. Niet aangeboden zolang hij niet veilig te stoppen is.","Not controlled by OpenThermostat. The Boiler page counts keep-warm runs, so you can see the effect.":"Niet geregeld door OpenThermostat. De ketelpagina telt de warmhoudbeurten, zodat je het effect ziet.","Not used by OpenThermostat. Not offered for modulating boilers.":"Niet gebruikt door OpenThermostat. Niet aangeboden voor modulerende ketels.","Not used by OpenThermostat. Not offered until its meaning is confirmed per model.":"Niet gebruikt door OpenThermostat. Niet aangeboden totdat de betekenis per model bevestigd is.","Off: no gas for hot water and no keep-warm runs, but also no hot water. A circulation pump stops as well.":"Uit: geen gas voor warm water en geen warmhoudbeurten, maar ook geen warm water. Een circulatiepomp stopt ook.","Off: the boiler ignores every heat request, also from OpenThermostat, until you switch it on again. Useful as a summer switch.":"Uit: de ketel negeert elke warmtevraag, ook van OpenThermostat, tot je hem weer aanzet. Handig als zomerschakelaar.","Off: the circulation pump never runs. That saves heat lost in the pipes, but hot water takes longer to reach the tap.":"Uit: de circulatiepomp draait nooit. Dat spaart warmte die in de leidingen verloren gaat, maar warm water doet er langer over om bij de kraan te komen.","On low-temperature boilers with a separate boiler controller (such as a Buderus MC10): the boiler temperature the water must reach before the pump starts.":"Bij lagetemperatuurketels met een losse ketelregelaar (zoals een Buderus MC10): de keteltemperatuur die het water moet halen voordat de pomp start.","On such a boiler a value that is too low may let flue gas condense inside a boiler that is not built for it. What it does on other boilers is unknown.":"Bij zo'n ketel kan een te lage waarde rookgas laten condenseren in een ketel die daar niet voor gebouwd is. Wat het bij andere ketels doet, is onbekend.","On: hot water reaches the taps sooner for a while. The boiler's own schedule takes over again later.":"Aan: warm water komt een tijdje sneller bij de kranen. Daarna neemt het eigen schema van de ketel het weer over.","On: slightly less gas per charge. The store may end just below its target.":"Aan: iets minder gas per oplaadbeurt. De boiler eindigt mogelijk net onder zijn doel.","One extra reheat. Handy before a bath when eco is on.":"Eén extra opwarmbeurt. Handig voor een bad als eco aan staat.","Only matters when a circulation pump is fitted. Long pauses leave lukewarm water standing in the pipes.":"Alleen van belang als er een circulatiepomp is. Lange pauzes laten lauw water in de leidingen staan.","Only matters while a disinfection runs. Higher: a shorter hold time, but more gas and more scale.":"Alleen van belang terwijl er een desinfectie loopt. Hoger: een kortere houdtijd, maar meer gas en meer kalk.","Only two-stage burners, mostly older floor-standing oil or gas boilers, use this. On a modulating wall-hung boiler nothing should change.":"Alleen tweetrapsbranders gebruiken dit, vooral oudere staande olie- of gasketels. Op een modulerende wandketel hoort er niets te veranderen.","OpenThermostat already keeps its own minimum on and off time for its request. This boiler timer works inside a running request.":"OpenThermostat houdt al een eigen minimale aan- en uittijd aan voor zijn vraag. Deze keteltimer werkt binnen een lopende vraag.","OpenThermostat does not control hot water, but the Boiler page counts keep-warm runs, so you can see the effect.":"OpenThermostat regelt warm water niet, maar de ketelpagina telt de warmhoudbeurten, zodat je het effect ziet.","OpenThermostat does not control hot water.":"OpenThermostat regelt warm water niet.","OpenThermostat does not limit burner power.":"OpenThermostat begrenst het brandervermogen niet.","OpenThermostat does not run the pump itself. This is one of the four Classic settings the E32 can read back.":"OpenThermostat stuurt de pomp niet zelf aan. Dit is een van de vier Classic-instellingen die de E32 kan teruglezen.","OpenThermostat keeps its own maximum per installation and never asks for more than this boiler limit.":"OpenThermostat houdt een eigen maximum per installatie aan en vraagt nooit meer dan deze ketelgrens.","OpenThermostat sends only a water temperature and leaves this part of the request alone. Never offered.":"OpenThermostat stuurt alleen een watertemperatuur en laat dit deel van de vraag met rust. Wordt nooit aangeboden.","OpenThermostat stops asking for heat by itself when no room needs it. It cannot override this switch.":"OpenThermostat vraagt zelf geen warmte als geen ruimte die nodig heeft. Deze schakelaar kan het niet omzeilen.","Restart margin for the second stage of a two-stage burner.":"Herstartmarge voor de tweede trap van een tweetrapsbrander.","Risk of scalding. EMS-ESP notes that stopping it this way does not seem to work; switching the boiler off and on stops it.":"Kans op verbranding. EMS-ESP meldt dat stoppen op deze manier niet lijkt te werken; de ketel uit- en aanzetten stopt hem.","Starts a thermal disinfection now: the boiler heats the hot water to the disinfection temperature and holds it there for a while. On this page the row shows whether one runs.":"Start nu een thermische desinfectie: de ketel warmt het warme water op tot de desinfectietemperatuur en houdt het daar een tijd. Op deze pagina toont de rij of er een loopt.","Switch-off margin for the second stage of a two-stage burner.":"Uitschakelmarge voor de tweede trap van een tweetrapsbrander.","Switches the circulation pump on or off now. It is a command, not a stored setting. On this page the row shows whether the pump runs.":"Zet de circulatiepomp nu aan of uit. Het is een opdracht, geen opgeslagen instelling. Op deze pagina toont de rij of de pomp draait.","Switching it on without a pump fitted does nothing useful. Long unused circulation pipes can hold lukewarm water.":"Aanzetten zonder pomp doet niets nuttigs. Lange, ongebruikte circulatieleidingen kunnen lauw water bevatten.","Tells the boiler whether a hot water circulation pump is fitted and may run.":"Vertelt de ketel of er een warmwatercirculatiepomp is en of die mag draaien.","The boiler follows the highest power or temperature request it receives. A value set by hand is replaced by the next request.":"De ketel volgt de hoogste vermogens- of temperatuurvraag die hij krijgt. Een met de hand gezette waarde wordt bij de volgende vraag vervangen.","The burner power a thermostat asks for right now, as part of the same live heat request.":"Het brandervermogen dat een thermostaat nu vraagt, als deel van dezelfde actuele warmtevraag.","The highest speed the boiler's heating pump may run at.":"De hoogste snelheid waarop de cv-pomp van de ketel mag draaien.","The highest water temperature the boiler sends to the heating, whatever a thermostat asks for.":"De hoogste watertemperatuur die de ketel naar de verwarming stuurt, wat een thermostaat ook vraagt.","The lowest speed the heating pump uses when the boiler runs at low power.":"De laagste snelheid die de cv-pomp gebruikt als de ketel op laag vermogen draait.","The shortest time the burner waits before it may start again for heating (anti-cycling).":"De kortste tijd dat de brander uit blijft voordat hij weer mag starten voor verwarming (anti-pendeltijd).","The temperature the boiler keeps the hot water at: the store, or the water from the tap on a combi boiler.":"De temperatuur waarop de ketel het warme water houdt: de boiler, of het tapwater bij een combiketel.","The temperature the boiler uses when it runs a thermal disinfection (against legionella) of the hot water.":"De temperatuur die de ketel gebruikt bij een thermische desinfectie (tegen legionella) van het warme water.","The water temperature a thermostat asks for right now (flow temperature). It is a live request, not a stored setting.":"De watertemperatuur die een thermostaat nu vraagt (aanvoertemperatuur). Het is een actuele vraag, geen opgeslagen instelling.","The wrong mode for the system can leave radiators or floor loops short of flow. Not every boiler has a pump that knows these modes.":"De verkeerde stand voor het systeem kan radiatoren of vloergroepen te weinig doorstroming geven. Niet elke ketel heeft een pomp die deze standen kent.","This is OpenThermostat's own heat request. It is never offered as a setting; only the attended boiler test uses it.":"Dit is de eigen warmtevraag van OpenThermostat. Het wordt nooit als instelling aangeboden; alleen de bijgewoonde keteltest gebruikt het.","Too low and rooms stay cold in winter. Too high is unsafe for floor heating without its own mixing valve and safety thermostat.":"Te laag en ruimtes blijven koud in de winter. Te hoog is onveilig voor vloerverwarming zonder eigen mengklep en maximaalthermostaat.","Too low and some rooms stay cold, or the boiler reaches its own limit sooner and switches on and off more.":"Te laag en sommige ruimtes blijven koud, of de ketel bereikt eerder zijn eigen grens en gaat vaker aan en uit.","Too low and the house cannot be kept warm on the coldest days. Hot water on a combi boiler may have its own limit.":"Te laag en het huis blijft op de koudste dagen niet warm. Warm water bij een combiketel heeft soms een eigen grens.","Too low and the store may never reach its target, which also weakens the protection against bacteria.":"Te laag en de boiler haalt zijn doel misschien nooit, wat ook de bescherming tegen bacteriën verzwakt.","Too low can give too little flow. The boiler water then heats up fast and the burner stops early.":"Te laag kan te weinig doorstroming geven. Het ketelwater wordt dan snel warm en de brander stopt vroeg.","Two devices that send different requests make the boiler switch on and off.":"Twee apparaten die verschillende vragen sturen, laten de ketel aan en uit schakelen.","Very short times let the boiler switch on and off often (short cycling). Very long times make rooms react slowly, especially with radiators.":"Erg korte tijden laten de ketel vaak aan en uit gaan (pendelen). Erg lange tijden maken dat ruimtes traag reageren, vooral met radiatoren.","While it is off, the house is not protected against frost. Only the boiler protects itself.":"Zolang hij uit staat, is het huis niet beschermd tegen vorst. Alleen de ketel beschermt zichzelf.","While the store charges, the burner stops a little early and the pump finishes the job with the heat that is left.":"Tijdens het opladen van de boiler stopt de brander iets eerder en maakt de pomp het af met de warmte die er nog is."})) if (!Object.hasOwn(messages, key)) messages[key] = value;
})();
